 HISTORY                                                          3031 1451
 -------                                                          3031 1451
 This evaluation was generated by Naval Nuclear Laboratory (Mar   3031 1451
 2023) [1] using the FLASSH code [2].  The physical model is      3031 1451
 based on a mixed elastic scattering treatment and includes       3031 1451
 coherent elastic scattering, incoherent elastic scattering and   3031 1451
 inelastic scattering components.  This evaluation is intended    3031 1451
 to be used with the companion H(7LiH) TSL evaluation when        3031 1451
 modeling enriched 7LiH.                                          3031 1451
                                                                  3031 1451
 THEORY                                                           3031 1451
 ------                                                           3031 1451
 Lithium hydride (LiH) has a fluorite (NaCl) type face-centered   3031 1451
 cubic crystal structure with four Li and  H atoms per unit       3031 1451
 cell.  The inelastic scattering cross sections were calculated   3031 1451
 in the incoherent approximations using the Li-7 partial phonon   3031 1451
 density of states from a VASP/PHONON calculation of 7LiH.  The   3031 1451
 LiH crystal structure and lattice constant from [3] were used    3031 1451
 in the VASP/PHONON calculation.  The mixed elastic scattering    3031 1451
 treatment was used to account for both coherent and incoherent   3031 1451
 elastic scattering effects in the material.  The coherent        3031 1451
 elastic scattering component was calculated in the cubic         3031 1451
 approximation using the FLASSH generalized coherent elastic      3031 1451
 scattering module using the 7LiH crystal structure and measured  3031 1451
 room temperature lattice constant of 4.0831 Ang from [3] along   3031 1451
 with free atom coherent scattering cross sections of 0.51 b for  3031 1451
 Li-7 and 0.439 b for H from [4].  The incoherent elastic         3031 1451
 scattering component was calculated using the Debye-Waller       3031 1451
 factor derived from the Li-7 partial phonon density of states    3031 1451
 and a Li-7 free atom incoherent scattering cross section of      3031 1451
 0.46 b.  A free atom total scattering cross section of 0.97 b    3031 1451
 was used to ensure consistency with the ENDF/B-VIII.1 Li-7       3031 1451
 evaluation.  A phonon order of 500 was used to ensure both the   3031 1451
 inelastic scattering cross section and the S(alpha,beta)         3031 1451
 functions at elevated temperatures were adaquately converged.    3031 1451
